        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `collapsible.tsx`, but I couldn't re-lint the file because running `oxlint` here needs approval. I checked the change by reading the code, not by a lint run.\n\nThe clickable header `div` (`collapsible.tsx:122`) now has:\n- **`role=\"button\"`**: clears `no-static-element-interactions` and tells screen readers it's a button.\n- **An `onKeyDown` handler**: Enter or Space calls `openTrigger()`, the same function a click calls. It also blocks Space from scrolling the page. This clears `click-events-have-key-events`.\n- **`tabIndex={0}`**: lets keyboard users tab to it, so the key handler can actually fire.\n- **`aria-expanded={open}`**: tells screen readers whether the section is open or closed.\n\nI didn't swap the `div` for a real `<button>`. The label passed in is an `<h3>`, and a heading isn't allowed inside a `<button>` in HTML. A `<button>` would also bring default browser styling that changes how the header looks.\n\nClicking works exactly as before. The only differences are that the header can now be focused and toggled from the keyboard, and screen readers announce it as a button.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "A `<button>` would also bring default browser styling that changes how the header looks."
        ],
