        "finalMessage": "I fixed the issue by replacing the `<div role=\"button\">` in `collapsible.tsx` with a real `<button type=\"button\">`. I couldn't run oxlint to confirm: both attempts to run it were blocked because they needed approval. Since the `role` attribute is gone, the rule should no longer fire.\n\nWhat changed in the header row:\n- **Kept:** `aria-expanded`, `className` and `onClick={openTrigger}`.\n- **Removed:** the `onKeyDown` Enter/Space handler, `tabIndex={0}` and `role=\"button\"`. A real button already takes focus and responds to Enter and Space, so clicking and keyboard use work the same as before.\n- **Added styles:** `background: \"none\"`, `border: 0`, `padding: 0`, `color`, `font` and `textAlign` set to `\"inherit\"`, and `width: \"100%\"`. These clear the browser's default button look so the row still looks like the old full-width flex `div`.\n\nThe new code has one HTML problem. Excalidraw passes `label={<h3>…</h3>}`, so there is now a heading inside a `<button>`. HTML doesn't allow that, and screen readers may not treat the `h3` as a heading inside a button. Browsers still display it correctly. The proper fix (a `<button>` inside the `<h3>`) means changing the code that calls this component in `Stats/index.tsx`, which was outside the one file I was allowed to edit.",
